    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q103-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Use the previous unit circle to show that\n$$1+\\tan^{2}\\theta=\\sec^{2}\\theta.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p6-q103-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1+\\tan^{2}\\theta=\\sec^{2}\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p6-q103-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply Pythagoras to ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\triangle OPA",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "OP^{2}+AP^{2}=OA^{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The radius $OP$ is perpendicular to the tangent $AP$. Also $OP=1$, $AP=\\tan\\theta$ and $OA=\\sec\\theta$. By Pythagoras,\n$$\\begin{align*}OP^{2}+AP^{2}&=OA^{2}\\\\1+\\tan^{2}\\theta&=\\sec^{2}\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q103-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Simplify $\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta-1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cot^{2}\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta-1&=\\frac{1}{\\sin^{2}\\theta}-1\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta-1&=\\frac{1-\\sin^{2}\\theta}{\\sin^{2}\\theta}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta-1&=\\frac{\\cos^{2}\\theta}{\\sin^{2}\\theta}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta-1&=\\cot^{2}\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nHere $\\sin^{2}\\theta+\\cos^{2}\\theta=1$ follows from Pythagoras on $\\triangle OXP$ in the unit-circle diagram.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q103-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Show that\n$$\\sec^{2}\\theta+\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta=(\\tan\\theta+\\cot\\theta)^{2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p6-q103-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sec^{2}\\theta+\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta=(\\tan\\theta+\\cot\\theta)^{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p6-q103-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply Pythagoras to ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\triangle OAB",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "AB=AP+PB=\\tan\\theta+\\cot\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Triangle $OAB$ is right-angled at $O$. From the diagram, $OA=\\sec\\theta$, $OB=\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta$ and $AB=AP+PB$, where $AP=\\tan\\theta$ and $PB=\\cot\\theta$. By Pythagoras,\n$$\\begin{align*}OA^{2}+OB^{2}&=AB^{2}\\\\\\sec^{2}\\theta+\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta&=(AP+PB)^{2}\\\\\\sec^{2}\\theta+\\operatorname{cosec}^{2}\\theta&=(\\tan\\theta+\\cot\\theta)^{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q103-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Write down a similar identity for $\\cot^{2}\\theta-\\cos^{2}\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cot^{2}\\theta-\\cos^{2}\\theta=(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-\\sin\\theta)^{2}$",
          "worked": "Triangle $BYP$ is right-angled at $Y$. Its lengths are $PB=\\cot\\theta$, $YP=\\cos\\theta$ and $BY=OB-OY=\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-\\sin\\theta$. By Pythagoras,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cot^{2}\\theta-\\cos^{2}\\theta&=BY^{2}\\\\\\cot^{2}\\theta-\\cos^{2}\\theta&=(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-\\sin\\theta)^{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q103-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Repeat for $\\tan^{2}\\theta-\\sin^{2}\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan^{2}\\theta-\\sin^{2}\\theta=(\\sec\\theta-\\cos\\theta)^{2}$",
          "worked": "Triangle $AXP$ is right-angled at $X$. Its lengths are $AP=\\tan\\theta$, $XP=\\sin\\theta$ and $AX=OA-OX=\\sec\\theta-\\cos\\theta$. By Pythagoras,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan^{2}\\theta-\\sin^{2}\\theta&=AX^{2}\\\\\\tan^{2}\\theta-\\sin^{2}\\theta&=(\\sec\\theta-\\cos\\theta)^{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
